page=release sect=6 summary="release records"
    src=build.c,cmd/install.c,servers/distd/distd.c
    keys=release,record,records,set,tree,arch,channel,commit,update

# SYNOPSIS

```ndb
release=N name=NAME channel=CHANNEL commit=COMMIT vx-abi=LEVELS unsigned
set=base arch=ARCH tree=b2:HASH size=BYTES
```

# DESCRIPTION

A release record says what one release of VectraOS is: its number, where it was built from, and the hash of each of its trees, one for each architecture.
It is ndb text (see ndb(6)): a first record about the release, then a record for each tree, which the record calls a set.
A tree's hash names its root directory in the content store, and through it every file of the release (see store(6)).

`./build release` writes one, `out/release/release.ndb`, after putting both architectures' base trees into `out/release/store`.
An install medium carries a record of its own, `records/`<n>`.ndb`, at the front of its store image, `store.tar`.
install(8) reads the medium's record (the last, if it carries more than one), installs the base tree it names for the machine's architecture, and copies the record into the system volume's `store` branch as `records/`<file>, keeping its name.
distd(8) reads every `records/*.ndb` in that branch, at the start and at `rescan`, and serves each as `/dist/releases/`<n>`/record`, exactly as it is.

Neither reader needs the records in order, nor the tuples in a record: each key is looked for in every record.
A record with a key not defined below is refused: install(8) fails, and distd(8) does not serve it.

## The release

: `release`
  The release's number, decimal: its sequence, which only grows.
  `./build release` writes the number of commits up to the one it builds, from `git rev-list --count HEAD`.
  distd names the release by it, and skips a record file without one; install writes it into the slot table (see slots(6)).
  When more than one record has it, the last is taken.
: `name`
  The release's name for people: `dev-`<n> from `./build release`.
  Not read.
: `channel`
  The channel the release is published on: `dev` from `./build release`.
  Not read.
: `commit`
  The git commit the release is built from, 40 hex digits, followed by `+dirty` if the working tree had changes.
  Not read.
: `vx-abi`
  The ABI levels the release provides, separated by commas: `0` while the ABI is a draft.
  Not read.
: `unsigned`
  A flag: the record has no signatures.
  Every record is unsigned today; the flag is not read.

## Sets

: `set`
  The set the record describes: `base`, the base system.
  Only `base` is read.
: `arch`
  The architecture the tree is for: `x86_64` or `aarch64`.
  install and distd each take the `set=base` record of their own architecture and ignore the others.
: `tree`
  The tree's hash, `b2:` and 64 hex digits: its root directory's name in the store.
  A record whose base tree for this architecture has no `tree`, or a malformed one, names no release for install, which refuses the medium, nor for distd, which skips it.
: `size`
  The bytes of the tree's files, decimal, as vxstore(8) counts them.
  Written by `./build release`, not by install media; not read.

# EXAMPLES

The record `./build release` wrote for release 174, built from a tree with uncommitted changes:

```ndb
release=174 name=dev-174 channel=dev
    commit=3e34a58a22f2815df0effada9816f017028f09e4+dirty vx-abi=0 unsigned
set=base arch=x86_64
    tree=b2:fb75fe2e7273a2973ace1435c4322d4cc93c108ebc51c1fc38b5f36ea536b6a2
    size=170704900
set=base arch=aarch64
    tree=b2:9573cfa899be6a89530d5f91ed9505fad792787122f79d92dbbb325921435c53
    size=175122380
```

An install medium's, as install(8) copies it into the store:

```ndb
release=2 name=test-2 channel=dev commit=test vx-abi=0 unsigned
set=base arch=x86_64
    tree=b2:6d7eccaf261abb486a2b201954baed8fe62ba8a253dfcae1877fbf61afa9dd16
```

# FILES

: `out/release/release.ndb`
  The record `./build release` writes.
: `records/<n>.ndb`
  An install medium's record, in its `store.tar`.
: `/n/records/*.ndb`
  The records in distd's namespace: the `store` branch of the system volume.
: `/dist/releases/<n>/record`
  A record as distd(8) serves it.

# SEE ALSO

distd(8), install(8), vxstore(8), store(6), slots(6), ndb(6); `docs/06-install-update.md` §5.3 in the repository

# BUGS

Records are not signed, and nothing checks them: the design's signatures, `prev` chain, `image=` records with `hash` and `sha256`, and heads records with `expires` and `revoked` are not written or read, and a node accepts any record in its store, older or newer.

A `release` that is not a number is ignored without a word: install then takes release 0, and distd skips the record.
distd reads at most 16 records, each at most 16 KiB, and names a release by the first record file it reads with that number.

`./build release --verify` compares the record as text, looking for `arch=`<arch>` tree=`<hash> followed by a space, so it fails on a record whose `tree` is the last tuple of its line, or which is written in another order.
